<%- include('partials/head', { meta: { title: 'FAQ', description: 'Frequently asked questions about Odyssey Retreats — travel, food, accommodations, registration, and more.' } }) %>
<body class="page-body">
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-bg" style="background-image: url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1426604966848-d7adac402bff?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&q=85')"></div>
  <div class="page-hero-overlay"></div>
  <div class="page-hero-content">
    <p class="t-eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px">Common Questions</p>
    <h1 class="t-title-lg">Frequently Asked <em>Questions</em></h1>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="faq-layout">

    <div class="faq-nav-sticky">
      <p class="faq-nav-label">Topics</p>
      <div class="faq-nav-links">
        <button class="faq-nav-link active" data-target="travel">Getting There</button>
        <button class="faq-nav-link" data-target="food">Food &amp; Dietary</button>
        <button class="faq-nav-link" data-target="accommodations">Accommodations</button>
        <button class="faq-nav-link" data-target="schedule">Schedule &amp; Format</button>
        <button class="faq-nav-link" data-target="registration">Registration</button>
        <button class="faq-nav-link" data-target="workshops">Workshops</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-content">

      <div class="faq-group" id="travel">
        <h2 class="faq-group-title">Getting There</h2>
        <div class="faq-items">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">How do I get to the camp retreats (Maryland or California)? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>After you register, you'll receive an email with all travel options and directions. For our Northern Maryland camp, the best airport is Baltimore/Washington International (BWI); the site is just off Route 95, about 30 minutes north of Baltimore, and is also accessible by public transportation. We recommend renting a car for the drive, though shuttle and carpool options are available after registration.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">How do I get to the hotel conventions (Baltimore or San Jose)? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>For our Baltimore Winter Convention at the Inner Harbor, we recommend flying into BWI, then taking the MARC train to the station directly across from the hotel, or an Uber for approximately $30. For our Bay Area Fall Convention in San Jose, fly into San Jose Airport or SFO, then take an Uber to the hotel. After registration, our hotel coordinator will be in touch to assist with your room reservation and answer any travel questions.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Is public transportation an option? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Our Northern Maryland camp is accessible by public transportation, though having your own car is recommended for flexibility during the weekend. Our California Sierra Nevada camp is roughly 2.5 hours from the Bay Area (about 2 hours from Sacramento) with no shuttle service, so a rental car is required. Both hotel conventions are easily reached by rideshare or, in Baltimore's case, the MARC train.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="food">
        <h2 class="faq-group-title">Food &amp; Dietary</h2>
        <div class="faq-items">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What will the food be like at the camp retreats? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Meals are served in the camp's dining hall, with breakfast, lunch, dinner, and a midnight snack available each day. The meal plan is optional — an add-on to your retreat fee — but highly recommended, since the camp locations are largely self-contained and off-site dining options are limited. Food service is similar at both our Maryland and California camp locations.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What about food at the hotel conventions? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Unlike the camp retreats, we don't offer a meal plan at the hotel conventions — both Baltimore and San Jose are large conference hotels surrounded by plenty of local restaurants, and most attendees dine on their own or with friends between sessions. We do coordinate group reservations for some meals during the weekend; details are shared after you register.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Are vegetarian or special dietary meals available? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Vegetarian options are always available with the camp meal plan, and our kitchen team will do their best to accommodate other dietary needs — just note them during registration. For hotel conventions, let us know about any dietary needs for the group meals we coordinate.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="accommodations">
        <h2 class="faq-group-title">Accommodations</h2>
        <div class="faq-items">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What are the cabins and lodge rooms like? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>The camps have a lodge with private rooms as well as private cabins, each with real beds and mattresses, full bathrooms with hot water, showers, flush toilets, and electricity for your alarm clock and coffee maker. These are comfortable private accommodations — not bunks or dormitories. You'll have everything you need for a comfortable stay.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Can we tent camp instead of using a cabin? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Absolutely. For those who prefer to get closer to nature, there are over 200 acres available to pitch a tent. You'll still have access to all the facilities, meals, workshops, and events.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What activities are available at the camp besides workshops? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>The camp offers a swimming pool, a private lake, nightly bonfires, and miles of hiking trails — all set within a beautiful 200-acre private facility. Many couples take advantage of the natural setting between sessions.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What are the hotel accommodations like? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Both hotel conventions are held at large, conference-style hotels with full amenities. Our San Jose hotel has a pool on-site. The Baltimore hotel doesn't have a pool, but it's right next to the Inner Harbor, with a plethora of restaurants and tourist attractions within walking distance.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="schedule">
        <h2 class="faq-group-title">Schedule &amp; Format</h2>
        <div class="faq-items">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">How long is a retreat? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>The core weekend package is 4 days, beginning on Friday and running through Monday. This allows full days of workshops and evening social events every day, including Sunday. We find that most couples appreciate the opportunity to continue working on Sunday rather than leaving early. Many guests depart Monday morning after a group brunch. Specific dates for each of our four retreats are listed on the Registration page.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Can we arrive earlier than Friday? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Many returning guests like to start their trip on Wednesday or Thursday and turn the retreat into a 5 or 6 day holiday vacation. This option is especially popular for those who want to enjoy the natural setting before the workshops begin.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What happens at the evening social events? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Evening social events typically run from 9pm to 1am and are a mix of structured activities and free socializing. These are fun, celebratory evenings where couples connect with others, relax, and enjoy themselves. Many lasting friendships are formed at our evening events.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="registration">
        <h2 class="faq-group-title">Registration</h2>
        <div class="faq-items">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What time should I arrive on the first day? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>There is no on-site registration — you must register and pay in advance on the Registration page before the retreat begins. On the first day of your retreat, on-site check-in and arrival runs from Noon to 9pm. We recommend registering online as soon as possible, as spots fill quickly, especially for the camp retreats.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Are day passes available? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. We offer day passes for those who absolutely cannot attend the full weekend, and for returning guests from previous years. We strongly recommend the full experience, but we understand that life's demands sometimes make that impossible. Contact us at <a href="mailto:<%= site.registrarEmail %>" style="color:var(--gold-dk)"><%= site.registrarEmail %></a> to ask about day pass availability.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Who should I contact with registration questions? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>For registration questions, please email <a href="mailto:<%= site.registrarEmail %>" style="color:var(--gold-dk)"><%= site.registrarEmail %></a> or call us at <%= site.phone %>. For general information, you can also reach us at <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>" style="color:var(--gold-dk)"><%= site.email %></a>.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-group" id="workshops">
        <h2 class="faq-group-title">Workshops</h2>
        <div class="faq-items">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Do we need to be in a troubled relationship to attend? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Absolutely not. Many of our couples are in happy, healthy relationships and simply want to go deeper or strengthen what they have. Our workshops are designed for all couples at all stages. The tools we teach are valuable whether you're newlyweds or have been together for decades.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">Are the workshops the same every year? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. We bring in different national presenters for each retreat, ensuring fresh perspectives and new techniques every time. Many of our returning guests tell us they discover something new at every retreat, no matter how many times they've attended.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question">What philosophical approach do the workshops take? <span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
            <div class="faq-answer"><p>Our educational staff is versed in traditional western psychological teachings as well as a wide variety of eastern philosophies. We weave both traditions together to provide a rich, multi-dimensional toolkit. You do not need any prior knowledge of either tradition to benefit from our workshops.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top:48px; padding:28px 32px; background:var(--warm-dk); border-left:2px solid var(--gold-dk)">
        <p class="t-body-warm" style="margin-bottom:12px">Have a question we didn't answer? We'd love to hear from you.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="m-link">Send us a message &#8594;</a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<script src="/js/main.js?v=<%= site.version %>"></script>
</body>
</html>
